xnu 0090: write support on the UFS root device

launchd's first boot task mounts / read-write and fails: the block device
has no write path (d_open returns EROFS for FWRITE, the strategy answers
EROFS to every B_WRITE, and the disk ioctls still describe read-only
media), so the root stays read-only and /private/var cannot be created.

Add the write half of the same path the reads use: WRITE(10) into the
bounce buffer, the data-out direction in the request descriptor and the
command UPIU, a read-modify-write for ranges that do not cover whole
2048-byte device blocks, and SYNCHRONIZE CACHE(10) after each transfer
(the device caches the writes). d_open accepts FWRITE and the character
device gets the matching physio. DKIOCISWRITABLE and the write limits now
describe a writable disk: HFS turns HFS_WRITEABLE_MEDIA on only when the
device says so, and the journal sizes its transfers from the limits. The
transfer is synchronous, as the reads already were.

